<Base title="About Orchard" desc="Orchard is an independent site about Apple. How we choose sources, label rumors and handle corrections." path="/about">
<p class="ol-k">About</p>
<h1 class="ol-title">About Orchard</h1>
<p class="ol-lead">Orchard keeps news, rumors, devices, events and iPhone Duo apps in tidy rows, each with its source.</p>
<div class="ol-cols"><div class="ol-body ol-stack">
<h2 class="ol-sh first">What this is</h2>
<p>An independent site about Apple. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Apple. “Apple”, “iPhone” and other product names belong to their owners and are used only to say what each page is about.</p>
<h2 class="ol-sh" id="how">How we work</h2>
<ul class="ol-list">
<li style="grid-template-columns:1fr"><div class="t">Apple first</div><div class="ol-src">When Apple has said something, we link Apple’s own page before anyone else’s.</div></li>
<li style="grid-template-columns:1fr"><div class="t">Rumors are labelled</div><div class="ol-src">A rumor keeps a Rumor label until Apple confirms it. The <a href="/rumors">rumor tracker</a> shows every outcome.</div></li>
<li style="grid-template-columns:1fr"><div class="t">Every claim has a source</div><div class="ol-src">Each story, device and app page lists where its facts came from.</div></li>
<li style="grid-template-columns:1fr"><div class="t">No invented numbers</div><div class="ol-src">If we do not have a price, date or spec, the page leaves it out.</div></li>
<li style="grid-template-columns:1fr"><div class="t">Our picks are our own ranking</div><div class="ol-src">The <a href="/picks">picks</a> rank apps from our record of how each uses the fold. They are not hands-on reviews.</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
